# tRPC hook destructuring

Name hooks after the **procedure** (last segment of the path), not the mutation/query object.

## useMutation

Always destructure `mutateAsync` as the procedure name. Pull `error` / `isPending` (or `isLoading`) only when used.

```tsx
// ✅
const { mutateAsync: minimize } = trpc.app.minimize.useMutation();
const { mutateAsync: check, isPending: checkPending, error: checkError } = trpc.update.check.useMutation();

await minimize();

// ❌
const minimize = trpc.app.minimize.useMutation();
minimize.mutateAsync();
const minimizeMutation = trpc.app.minimize.useMutation();
```

## useQuery

Destructure `data` as the procedure name. Pull `error` / `isPending` / `isLoading` only when used.

```tsx
// ✅
const { data: isWin11 } = trpc.app.isWin11.useQuery();
const { data: updateInfo = null, isPending: updatePending } = trpc.update.get.useQuery();

// ❌
const updateQuery = trpc.update.get.useQuery();
updateQuery.data;
const { data } = trpc.update.get.useQuery(); // unnamed / generic
```

## Notes

- Alias = procedure key: `trpc.track.togglePlay` → `mutateAsync: togglePlay`
- Defaults on `data` OK: `data: updateDownloaded = false`
- Subscriptions stay `useSubscription`; this rule is for query/mutation only
